<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The two launcher surfaces outside the app: the three static app shortcuts on a
    long press of the icon, and the quick settings tile. MASTER_BUILD_PROMPT 13.5,
    design-v3.md 12.4.

    **Fixed interface labels only**, exactly as strings.xml is. Nothing here is an
    observation about a person, and nothing on either surface is composed: a shortcut
    label is a destination's name and the tile says which of its two things a tap
    would do. Neither surface can reach the engine and neither has anything to say
    about anybody's week.

    **A second values file rather than lines in strings.xml, and the reason is the
    day this was written.** Three builders were in this tree at once and strings.xml
    was open in two of them. Resource merging does not care which file in values/ a
    name arrives from, so the merge conflict is worth avoiding and the split costs
    nothing but this comment. Everything here is a launcher surface, which is at
    least a real seam and not an arbitrary one.
-->
<resources>

    <!--
        The three static shortcuts, MASTER_BUILD_PROMPT 13.5 and design-v3.md 12.4.

        **The short label and the long label are the same three names**, because those
        names are specified. A launcher shows the long label where it fits and falls
        back to the short one where it does not, so a longer, more descriptive long
        label would be the string most people actually see, and the three names the
        design chose would appear only on a narrow screen. Sentence case, no counts,
        and nothing that reports on the person.
    -->
    <string name="shortcut_capture_short">Quick capture</string>
    <string name="shortcut_capture_long">Quick capture</string>
    <string name="shortcut_focus_short">Start focus</string>
    <string name="shortcut_focus_long">Start focus</string>
    <string name="shortcut_pulse_short">Today\'s Pulse</string>
    <string name="shortcut_pulse_long">Today\'s Pulse</string>

    <!--
        The quick settings tile, MASTER_BUILD_PROMPT 13.5 and design-v3.md 12.4.

        `tile_focus_name` is the fixed name in the shade's tile picker, where the tile
        is being chosen rather than used and has no state to reflect yet. The two
        labels below it are the live ones, and which of them shows is the whole of what
        the tile knows: a session is running, or one is not.
    -->
    <string name="tile_focus_name">Focus session</string>
    <string name="tile_focus_start">Start focus</string>
    <string name="tile_focus_end">End focus</string>

    <!--
        Read instead of the label by TalkBack, per design-v3.md 13. A sentence rather
        than a label, which is the same rule the widgets' content descriptions follow.
        Neither names the item: the shade is readable over a lock screen, and what a
        person is working on is not for whoever is holding the phone.
    -->
    <string name="cd_tile_focus_start">Start a focus session</string>
    <string name="cd_tile_focus_end">End the focus session that is running</string>
</resources>
